---
import SlideChrome from '../SlideChrome.astro';
---

<SlideChrome>
	<div class="flex h-full flex-col">
		<h2 class="pitch-title">Audience &amp; Cultural Timing</h2>
		<p class="pitch-subtitle">HYPE targets two proven player audiences</p>
		<div class="mt-[clamp(1.25rem,4vh,2.5rem)] grid flex-1 grid-cols-2 gap-6 md:gap-12">
			<section>
				<h3 class="pitch-bold text-[clamp(0.85rem,1.5vw,1.15rem)]">Co-op horror players</h3>
				<p class="pitch-muted mt-4 text-[clamp(0.65rem,1.1vw,0.85rem)]">Why they care:</p>
				<p class="pitch-body mt-1">
					Readable objectives, social pressure, panic, teamwork, failure stories, and repeatable sessions.
				</p>
				<p class="pitch-muted mt-4 text-[clamp(0.65rem,1.1vw,0.85rem)]">Proof direction:</p>
				<p class="pitch-body mt-1">
					Lethal Company, and R.E.P.O. show strong demand for social horror built around group chaos.
				</p>
			</section>
			<section>
				<h3 class="pitch-bold text-[clamp(0.85rem,1.5vw,1.15rem)]">Supernatural anime fans</h3>
				<p class="pitch-muted mt-4 text-[clamp(0.65rem,1.1vw,0.85rem)]">Why they care:</p>
				<p class="pitch-body mt-1">
					Ordinary students, strange occult cases, comedy-horror escalation, and emotional supernatural stakes.
				</p>
				<p class="pitch-muted mt-4 text-[clamp(0.65rem,1.1vw,0.85rem)]">Proof direction:</p>
				<p class="pitch-body mt-1">
					DAN DA DAN and Mob Psycho 100 prove modern supernatural anime can reach mainstream scale without losing its
					weird, high-energy occult identity.
				</p>
				<p class="mt-4 text-[clamp(0.55rem,0.95vw,0.72rem)] leading-relaxed text-white/90 underline decoration-white/70 underline-offset-2">
					DAN DA DAN: 96.5M hours watched + 19.6M views in NETFLIX
				</p>
				<p class="mt-1 text-[clamp(0.55rem,0.95vw,0.72rem)] leading-relaxed text-white/90 underline decoration-white/70 underline-offset-2">
					Mob Psycho 100: 2.8M+ manga copies sold
				</p>
			</section>
		</div>
		<p class="pitch-body mt-auto pt-4 text-center">
			HYPE connects anime-supernatural fantasy with the proven formal of co-op horror.
		</p>
	</div>
</SlideChrome>
